# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Intentfile (A2ML Canonical) — north-star contractile
#
# Paired runner: intend.ncl
# Verb:          intend
#
# Semantics: North-star contractile. Declares BOTH concrete committed
#            next-actions AND horizon aspirations the project wishes to
#            become. Two sections share one file because they answer
#            the same question at different ranges:
#              [[intents]] — "we WILL do this; track progress"
#                            status: declared → in_progress → done |
#                                    deferred | retired
#              [[wishes]]  — "we WISH this were true; revisit later"
#                            status: declared → in_progress → achieved |
#                                    abandoned
#                            grouped by horizon: near / mid / far.
#            Non-gating — this is a report, not a gate. See the `must`
#            contractile for hard gates.

@abstract:
North-star contractile for stateful-artefacts: the state-carrying
artefact layer of the Reposystem/OPSM stack. Declares what the project
IS (purpose), what it is NOT (anti-purpose), and its committed
next-actions and aspirational wishes.
@end

## Purpose

Stateful Artefacts provides one canonical, machine-readable state schema
(identity, provenance, lifecycle phase, verification status) carried by the
artefacts the hyperpolymath estate produces and consumes — graph exports,
scenario states, estate metadata, VeriSimDB feed records — plus the tooling
to read, write, and validate those records across languages via a
formally-typed C ABI. (PROVISIONAL — refine on content re-transfer from
hyperpolymath/reposystem.)

## Anti-Purpose

This repository is NOT:
- A general-purpose metadata framework (it serves the estate's artefact-state schema, nothing broader)
- The Reposystem graph engine itself (that remains in hyperpolymath/reposystem)
- A database (VeriSimDB in hyperpolymath/nextgen-databases is the aggregation sink; this layer only emits/validates records)

## If In Doubt

If you are unsure whether a change is in scope, ask. Sensitive areas:
the ABI surface (`src/interface/`), the state-record schema, and anything
touching licensing (MPL-2.0 vs reposystem's PMPL-1.0 is unresolved).

## Committed Next-Actions

### abi-seam-builds
- description: The Idris2↔Zig ABI seam compiles and its unit + integration tests pass
- probe: cd src/interface/ffi && zig build test
- status: done
- notes: Symbol prefix stateful_artefacts_*; Result canon shared by both sides; 16 Zig tests pass

### v0-artefact-state-record
- description: v0 record (schema + Zig core + lifecycle proofs) through the seam
- probe: cd src/interface/ffi && zig build test && bash tests/aspect_tests.sh
- status: done
- notes: docs/spec/ARTEFACT-STATE-RECORD.adoc; src/core/record.zig; Abi/Record.idr; ArtefactLifecycle.tla. PROVISIONAL, additive-only. Idris2/TLC checks are CI-gated.

### retransfer-domain-content
- description: Re-transfer the stateful-artefacts slice out of hyperpolymath/reposystem into src/core
- probe: test -n "$(find src/core -name '*.rs' | head -1)"
- status: declared
- notes: Blocked on maintainer access to $REPOS_DIR; reconcile with the v0 record; see README re-transfer checklist

